  "task": "Write Python 3 function solve(rows). First apply an audit filter to the ORIGINAL input positions, indexed from zero: omit positions whose index modulo 5 equals 4, except always retain the last input position. Rotate the retained rows LEFT by 3 positions modulo the retained length (empty stays empty). Apply the following rules to that transformed list: Rows [expiry,quantity] describe lots. Today is day 12. Include a lot only if expiry is STRICTLY later than today. Return total quantity and the earliest eligible expiry as [quantity,expiry], using null expiry if none.\nReturn the requested value, without printing. Inputs follow the types specified. Do not mutate the input. Standard library is allowed.",
  "specification": "First apply an audit filter to the ORIGINAL input positions, indexed from zero: omit positions whose index modulo 5 equals 4, except always retain the last input position. Rotate the retained rows LEFT by 3 positions modulo the retained length (empty stays empty). Apply the following rules to that transformed list: Rows [expiry,quantity] describe lots. Today is day 12. Include a lot only if expiry is STRICTLY later than today. Return total quantity and the earliest eligible expiry as [quantity,expiry], using null expiry if none.",
  "reference": "def solve(rows):\n good=[(e,q) for e,q in rows if e>12]\n return [sum(q for e,q in good),min((e for e,q in good),default=None)]\n_core_solve=solve\ndef solve(rows):\n filtered=[row for i,row in enumerate(rows) if i%5!=4 or i==len(rows)-1]\n if filtered:\n  shift=3%len(filtered)\n  filtered=filtered[shift:]+filtered[:shift]\n return _core_solve(filtered)",
  "mutation": "def solve(rows):\n good=[(e,q) for e,q in rows if e>=12]\n return [sum(q for e,q in good),min((e for e,q in good),default=None)]\n_core_solve=solve\ndef solve(rows):\n filtered=[row for i,row in enumerate(rows) if i%5!=4 or i==len(rows)-1]\n if filtered:\n  shift=3%len(filtered)\n  filtered=filtered[shift:]+filtered[:shift]\n return _core_solve(filtered)",
